# A coding agent asks to keep working with the lid closed. You allow it from the
# menu, close the lid and leave; when the work ends, the Mac goes to sleep.
clock 21:04 · battery 64 · floor 15
process 4127 claude

$ awake -w 4127 --lid
caption "claude asks awake to keep the Mac up while it works, lid closed included."
open menu
caption "The question waits in the menu. Nothing changes until you answer it."
hover "Allow while it runs"
click "Allow while it runs"
caption "The cup burns: while claude runs, closing the lid will not sleep the Mac."

lid close
time +2h14m · battery 38
caption "Two hours later the lid is still shut, and the work goes on."
exit 4127
caption "The work ends. With nothing left holding it, the Mac goes to sleep."
lid open
caption "The banner saying why is waiting when you come back."
$ awake status
